    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Nestled in the peaceful countryside of Ballydavid, this beautifully maintained 3-bedroom home offers the perfect balance of comfort, charm, and stunning natural surroundings. Situated along the spectacular Wild Atlantic Way on the northerly side of the Dingle Peninsula, and positioned between Mount Brandon and Smerwick Harbour, the property enjoys breathtaking mountain views along with distant sea views towards the Three Sisters.\r\n\r\nInside, the home is bright, warm, and thoughtfully laid out. There are three generously proportioned bedrooms, including a spacious master bedroom complete with an en-suite bathroom and a walk-in wardrobe. The second bedroom is exceptionally large and offers excellent flexibility for family living, guests, or a home office space.\r\n\r\nThe sunny galley kitchen is full of character and features a raised breakfast bar, creating a welcoming heart to the home. A separate dining area sits to the rear of the cosy sitting room, where patio doors open to the outdoors and a fireplace adds warmth and atmosphere. Wood flooring throughout enhances the sense of quality and continuity within the home.\r\n\r\nFurther adding to the home’s appeal, solar panels provide excellent energy efficiency, offering a more sustainable and cost-effective way of living.\r\n\r\nOutside, the impressive grounds provide both practicality and lifestyle appeal, with two storage sheds, a polytunnel, a large kennel, and a separate wild garden area previously used for hens — ideal for gardening enthusiasts or those seeking a more self-sufficient lifestyle.\r\n\r\nThe location offers an exceptional coastal lifestyle. Duinín Pier is just a 15-minute walk away, while Ballydavid village is only a 5-minute drive and offers local pubs, an outdoor beach sauna, and wellness experiences including seaweed baths and massage treatments. The stunning Muiríoch Beach, a beautiful 3.4km stretch of coastline, is also just minutes away. Convenient access to the TFI Local Link at the end of the road provides easy connections to Dingle and beyond.\r\n\r\nSet in a tranquil and scenic setting, this property offers a rare opportunity to enjoy country living surrounded by some of Kerry’s most spectacular scenery while remaining close to local amenities and the vibrant atmosphere of Dingle."
      },
